From 4c19c168cd71fa7e1f4d7d739a553a1c72da32c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bruno Brito <brunocfbrito@github>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 21:20:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cavemem: scope search and session-start to current cwd
 (upstream bug #39)

Cherry-picked verbatim from upstream JuliusBrussee/cavemem PR #21
(BrunoCFBrito:fix/project-scoped-search), which is the unreviewed
fix for the cross-project session-start context leak tracked as
bug #39.

Upstream bug:    #39 (session-start cross-project context leak)
Source PR:       #21  https://github.com/JuliusBrussee/cavemem/pull/21
Source commit:   4c19c168cd71fa7e1f4d7d739a553a1c72da32c5
Source file(s):  packages/core/src/memory-store.ts
                 packages/hooks/src/handlers/session-start.ts
                 packages/storage/src/storage.ts

The PR predates upstream tag v0.2.1 (it was opened 2026-04-30 against
main at sha 72f27b3, before the v0.2.1 cut on 2026-05-06), but the
v0.2.1 release only modified apps/mcp-server/ and apps/cli/ (PR #16,
the MCP boot fix). None of the three files touched by this patch were
changed between PR #21's base and v0.2.1, so the diff applies cleanly.

Verified to apply cleanly with `patch -p1` and `git apply --check`
against the v0.2.1 source tarball
(https://api.github.com/repos/JuliusBrussee/cavemem/tarball/v0.2.1).

Original upstream commit message follows below the `---` separator.

Three changes to prevent cross-project memory pollution:

1. storage.ts — searchFts now accepts an optional cwd param; when set,
   the SQL joins sessions and filters by s.cwd = ? so BM25 results
   stay scoped to the current project.

2. memory-store.ts — MemoryStore tracks currentCwd on each
   startSession() call and passes it through to searchFts.

3. session-start.ts — prior-session context hints are now filtered
   by matching cwd, so a session in project A never gets injected
   with summaries from project B.

Co-Authored-By: DeepSeek v4 Pro <noreply@openclaude.dev>
